{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJiuqHuVBMMfE3UMoUSmpy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for submission ===\n3\t  # Post-Dream revision: added baseline experiments (exp-012~015) as highest priority\n4\t\n5\t  # --- Baselines (Dream-critical: make-or-break for paper acceptance) ---\n6\t\n7\t  - id: exp-012\n8\t    name: baseline_logprob\n9\t    claim: 1\n10\t    description: >\n11\t      Compute sequence log-probability for all existing pilot samples (SciERC NER+RE)\n12\t      and new dataset pilots. Correlate log-prob with F1 (ρ, AUROC, τ).\n13\t      If SJ does NOT beat log-prob, the 16x inference cost is unjustified and\n14\t      paper contribution weakens drastically. THIS IS THE MAKE-OR-BREAK EXPERIMENT.\n15\t    priority: P0\n16\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n17\t    deps: []\n18\t    note: >\n19\t      Needs vLLM forward pass to extract log-probs from existing samples.\n20\t      ~1h per dataset on 1 GPU. For new datasets, capture log-probs during pilot inference.\n21\t      Also compute on pilot_004/005 existing data if log-probs weren't saved.\n22\t\n23\t  - id: exp-013\n24\t    name: baseline_exact_match\n25\t    claim: 1\n26\t    description: >\n27\t      Exact-match voting rate: what fraction of N samples produce identical\n28\t      entity/relation sets? Correlate with F1. This is the direct analogue\n29\t      of Wang et al.'s original self-consistency for structured outputs.\n30\t    priority: P0\n31\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n32\t    deps: []\n33\t    note: CPU-only on existing pilot data. Zero cost.\n34\t\n35\t  - id: exp-014\n36\t    name: baseline_entity_voting\n37\t    claim: 1\n38\t    description: >\n39\t      Entity-level majority voting: for each entity, count how many of N\n40\t      samples include it. Select entities above threshold. Compare F1 of\n41\t      entity-voting selection vs SJ selection vs FK selection.\n42\t    priority: P0\n43\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n44\t    deps: []\n45\t    note: CPU-only on existing pilot data. Zero cost.\n46\t\n47\t  - id: exp-015\n48\t    name: evaluation_metrics_expansion\n49\t    claim: 1,2\n50\t    description: >\n51\t      Add AUROC (binary: good/bad output at threshold), calibration plots,\n52\t      and Kendall's τ alongside Spearman ρ for ALL confidence signals\n53\t      (SJ, FK, log-prob, exact-match, entity-voting) on ALL datasets.\n54\t      Also add leave-one-out SJ as robustness check for evaluation circularity.\n55\t    priority: P0\n56\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n57\t    deps: [exp-012, exp-013, exp-014]\n58\t    note: CPU-only analysis. Addresses Dream concerns D5 (single metric) and D17 (circularity).\n59\t\n60\t  # --- Core experiments ---\n61\t\n62\t  - id: exp-001\n63\t    name: ner_n16_scierc\n64\t    claim: 1\n65\t    description: >\n66\t      NER N=16 on SciERC (ft_002_v2 model). Strengthen rho estimation,\n67\t      test N-scaling. Run with seeds [42, 123, 456] for robustness.\n68\t      MUST capture log-probs during inference for exp-012.\n69\t    priority: P0\n70\t    gpu_budget_hours: 18\n71\t    deps: []\n72\t    dataset: SciERC\n73\t    model: ft_002_v2\n74\t    note: 3 seeds × 6h each. Inference script MUST output log-probs.\n75\t\n76\t  - id: exp-002\n77\t    name: ner_conll2003\n78\t    claim: 1\n79\t    description: >\n80\t      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003 (LoRA) + NER pilot (N=8, T=0.7).\n81\t      Cross-dataset generalization. MUST capture log-probs.\n82\t      Use consistent N and T with other datasets.\n83\t    priority: P0\n84\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n85\t    deps: []\n86\t    dataset: CoNLL-2003\n87\t    model: qwen3-8b (new fine-tune)\n88\t\n89\t  - id: exp-003\n90\t    name: ner_wnut17\n91\t    claim: 1\n92\t    description: >\n93\t      Fine-tune Qwen3-8B on WNUT-17 (LoRA) + NER pilot (N=8, T=0.7).\n94\t      Social media domain — cross-dataset generalization. MUST capture log-probs.\n95\t    priority: P0\n96\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n97\t    deps: []\n98\t    dataset: WNUT-17\n99\t    model: qwen3-8b (new fine-tune)\n100\t    note: User confirmed public datasets only.\n101\t\n102\t  - id: exp-004\n103\t    name: re_diagnostic_analysis\n104\t    claim: 2\n105\t    description: >\n106\t      Per-relation-type consistency breakdown on existing pilot_004/005 data.\n107\t      Error propagation patterns. Bootstrap CI for ALL rho comparisons.\n108\t      Add conditional threshold sensitivity analysis (vary exclusion criterion).\n109\t      Compare ALL confidence signals (SJ, FK, log-prob, exact-match) on RE.\n110\t    priority: P0\n111\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n112\t    deps: [exp-012, exp-013]\n113\t    note: CPU-only. Bootstrap CI + threshold sensitivity address Dream concerns.\n114\t\n115\t  - id: exp-005\n116\t    name: temperature_sensitivity_analysis\n117\t    claim: 2\n118\t    description: >\n119\t      T=0.7 vs T=1.0 comparison on both NER and RE for ALL confidence signals.\n120\t      Signal-noise tradeoff analysis.\n121\t    priority: P0\n122\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n123\t    deps: [exp-012]\n124\t    note: CPU-only on existing pilot_004 (T=1.0) and pilot_005 (T=0.7) data.\n125\t\n126\t  - id: exp-006\n127\t    name: adaptive_compute_demo\n128\t    claim: 1\n129\t    description: >\n130\t      Best-of-N selection on NER: SJ vs log-prob vs FK vs exact-match vs random vs greedy.\n131\t      Report on ALL NER datasets (not just SciERC). Include RE results too (even if negative).\n132\t    priority: P0\n133\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n134\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-012]\n135\t    note: CPU-only. Must cover all datasets and include RE for completeness.\n136\t\n137\t  - id: exp-007\n138\t    name: ner_multi_model\n139\t    claim: 1\n140\t    description: >\n141\t      NER pilot with LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct on SciERC. Model-agnostic validation.\n142\t      MUST capture log-probs for baseline comparison.\n143\t    priority: P0\n144\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n145\t    deps: []\n146\t    dataset: SciERC\n147\t    model: llama-3.1-8b (new fine-tune)\n148\t\n149\t  # === P1: Important, time permitting ===\n150\t\n151\t  - id: exp-008\n152\t    name: re_n16_confirmation\n153\t    claim: 2\n154\t    description: >\n155\t      RE N=16 on SciERC to confirm negative finding with higher statistical power.\n156\t    priority: P1\n157\t    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n158\t    deps: []\n159\t    dataset: SciERC\n160\t    model: ft_002_v2\n161\t\n162\t  - id: exp-009\n163\t    name: capability_stratification\n164\t    claim: 2\n165\t    description: >\n166\t      Stratify instances by difficulty (greedy F1 buckets + independent proxies:\n167\t      sentence length, entity count) for both NER and RE. Verify inverted-U pattern\n168\t      with proper statistical tests and independent stratification variable.\n169\t    priority: P1\n170\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n171\t    deps: [exp-001]\n172\t    note: CPU-only. Dream flagged inverted-U overclaiming — use independent proxy.\n173\t\n174\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n175\t\n176\t  - id: exp-010\n177\t    name: selection_curves\n178\t    claim: 1\n179\t    description: >\n180\t      Best-of-N selection curves for N=1,2,4,8,16 comparing all confidence signals.\n181\t      Visualize as line plots (not just tables — Dream flagged table-only presentation).\n182\t    priority: P2\n183\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n184\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-012]\n185\t    note: CPU-only visualization\n186\t\n187\t  - id: exp-011\n188\t    name: ner_ood_robustness\n189\t    claim: 1\n190\t    description: >\n191\t      Test NER consistency signal on OOD instances (cross-domain transfer).\n192\t    priority: P2\n193\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n194\t    deps: [exp-003]\n195\t\n196\t# GPU Budget Summary (post-Dream revision):\n197\t# P0: 54 GPU-hours (exp-012: 3h, exp-001: 18h, exp-002: 8h, exp-003: 10h, exp-007: 15h, rest: 0h)\n198\t# P1: 12 GPU-hours (exp-008: 12h, exp-009: 0h)\n199\t# P2: 5 GPU-hours (exp-010: 0h, exp-011: 5h)\n200\t# Total P0: 54 GPU-hours\n201\t# Available: 8x RTX 5090 = ~192 GPU-hours/day → P0 completable in ~1 day with parallel execution\n202\t#\n203\t# CRITICAL PATH: exp-012 (log-prob baseline) determines if SJ contribution is strong or weak.\n204\t# Run exp-012 on existing SciERC data ASAP — result informs whether to proceed with current framing.\n205\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0156ax1NzDJVhoRiaWcQ6P7T","session_id":"36d6115a-ae29-42f3-9a64-d29d87dc39c5","uuid":"9d58a450-5459-4255-8a09-4c35c7049af2","timestamp":"2026-05-14T11:13:39.155Z"}
