{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156ax1NzDJVhoRiaWcQ6P7T","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary of Experiment Data and Code Structure\n\nI've thoroughly explored the repository and compiled the following comprehensive report:\n\n### **1. EXPERIMENT PLAN FILE**\n- **Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/experiment_plan.yaml`\n- **Status**: Complete with prioritized experiments (P0, P1, P2)\n- **Key Experiments**:\n  - **exp-012** (baseline_logprob) — Make-or-break: compute sequence log-probability and correlate with F1 (ρ, AUROC, τ)\n  - **exp-013** (baseline_exact_match) — Exact-match voting rate CPU-only\n  - **exp-014** (baseline_entity_voting) — Entity-level majority voting comparison\n  - **exp-015** (evaluation_metrics_expansion) — AUROC, calibration, Kendall τ for all signals\n  - **exp-001** (ner_n16_scierc) — N=16 sampling on SciERC with log-probs\n  - **exp-002/003** (ner_conll2003/wnut17) — Cross-dataset NER with new fine-tunes\n  - **exp-004** (re_diagnostic_analysis) — Per-relation-type analysis with all confidence signals\n  - **exp-005** (temperature_sensitivity_analysis) — T=0.7 vs T=1.0 comparison\n\n---\n\n### **2. PYTHON CODE MODULES FOR METRICS**\n\n#### **Evaluation Module**\n- **Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/evaluation.py`\n- **Functions**:\n  - `compute_ner_f1()` — Micro-averaged NER precision/recall/F1\n  - `compute_re_f1()` — Relation extraction F1\n  - `per_instance_f1()` — Per-sample F1 for ner/re/eae\n  - `compute_sample_f1_distribution()` — F1 stats (mean, std, pct_zero)\n  - `spearman_correlation()` — Computes Spearman ρ and p-values\n  - `generate_evaluation_report()` — Comprehensive report with greedy/oracle/correlations\n\n#### **Consistency Module**\n- **Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/consistency.py`\n- **Functions**:\n  - `fleiss_kappa_surface()` — Surface-level Fleiss κ (entity_text, entity_type)\n  - `structural_consistency_soft_jaccard()` — Span-level soft Jaccard with Hungarian matching\n  - `_ner_soft_jaccard_pair()` — Type-aware soft Jaccard for NER\n  - `_re_soft_jaccard_pair()` — Relation soft Jaccard (head_span × tail_span × type_match)\n  - `oracle_best_of_n()` — Selects best sample by F1\n  - `compute_all_consistency_scores()` — Returns fleiss_kappa, soft_jaccard, oracle_f1, oracle_indices\n\n#### **Sampling & Inference**\n- **Path**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/sampling.py`\n- **Key**: VLLMSampler class for batch sampling with XGrammar constrained JSON output, UIE_JSON_SCHEMA defined\n\n---\n\n### **3. PILOT EXPERIMENT DATA & RESULTS**\n\n#### **mvp_pilot_001** (DONE, NEGATIVE)\n- **Status**: FAIL — RE ρ_sj=0.2535 < 0.40 threshold\n- **Data**: 551 instances, N=8 samples, T=1.0, SciERC ft_001\n- **Key Metrics**:\n  - **NER**: ρ_sj=0.3616 (strong), oracle F1=0.78, headroom=16.9pp\n  - **RE**: ρ_sj=0.2535 (weak), oracle F1=0.572, headroom=21.7pp\n  - SJ > κ on NER but NOT on RE full set\n  - Sample F1 pct_zero: NER=20.4%, RE=58.3%\n- **Verdict**: RE structural signal fundamentally weak\n\n#### **mvp_pilot_003** (DONE, NEGATIVE)\n- Same model as pilot_001 but improved parse handling\n- **RE**: ρ_sj=0.2367 < threshold, conditional ρ_sj=0.3004\n- **Confirmed**: RE signal limitation is structural, not parsing\n\n#### **mvp_pilot_004** (DONE, NEGATIVE)\n- **Model**: ft_002_v2 (improved RE F1=41.8%)\n- **Data**: 551 instances, N=8, T=1.0\n- **Key Metrics**:\n  - **NER**: ρ_sj=0.3825 (consistent), oracle F1=0.7756\n  - **RE full**: ρ_sj=0.2441 (κ=0.2782 beats SJ!), oracle F1=0.5882\n  - RE sample F1 pct_zero=44.3% (high failure rate)\n  - **Critical finding**: κ > SJ on RE full set (-0.034 Δ)\n- **Framing Impact**: NER-primary strategy preferred over RE-primary\n\n#### **mvp_pilot_005** (DONE, NEGATIVE)\n- Same model as pilot_004 but **T=0.7** (lower temperature)\n- **Data**: 551 instances, N=8\n- **Key Metrics**:\n  - **NER**: ρ_sj=0.3875 (similar), headroom=9.66pp (reduced)\n  - **RE full**: ρ_sj=0.2343 (worse than T=1.0!), κ=0.1835 (also drops)\n  - **RE conditional**: ρ_sj=0.3716 (good on filtered set)\n  - RE sample F1 pct_zero=42.4% (unchanged from T=1.0)\n- **Conclusion**: Temperature irrelevant; zero-rate rooted in model capacity\n\n#### **e1_component_wise_re_sj** (DONE, ANALYSIS)\n- **Analysis**: Decomposed RE SJ into head_sj, tail_sj, type_match\n- **Finding**: head_sj ρ=0.21 FAR below NER ρ=0.383 (Δ=-0.173)\n- **Verdict**: Multiplicative penalty hypothesis REJECTED; problem is fundamental\n- **Diagnosis**: Span-level SJ lacks discriminative power for RE relations\n\n#### **exp_012_logprob_baseline** (DONE, SUCCESS)\n- **Purpose**: Baseline comparison for SJ against log-probability\n- **Key Results**:\n  - **NER Full (n=529)**: SJ ρ=0.3565 >> logprob ρ=0.1396, AUROC 0.689 vs 0.591\n  - **NER Cond (n=501)**: SJ ρ=0.4120 >> logprob ρ=0.1627, AUROC 0.706 vs 0.597\n  - **RE Full (n=397)**: logprob ρ=0.2467 > SJ ρ=0.2112 (marginal), but κ ρ=0.2528 beats both\n  - **RE Cond (n=296)**: SJ ρ=0.3683 >> logprob ρ=0.1457\n- **Metrics Computed**: Spearman ρ, Kendall τ, AUROC, p-values\n- **Report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/exp_012_logprob_baseline/report/analysis_report.json`\n\n---\n\n### **4. REGISTRY & EXPERIMENT TRACKING**\n- **Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml`\n- **Experiments tracked**:\n  - ft_001, ft_002, ft_002_v2 (fine-tuning jobs)\n  - mvp_pilot_001/002/003/004/005 (MVP pilots)\n  - e1_component_wise_re_sj (diagnostic analysis)\n  - exp_012_logprob_baseline (log-prob baseline)\n- **Status tracking**: DONE/NEGATIVE/FAIL/SUCCESS with full metrics per experiment\n\n---\n\n### **5. KEY FINDINGS & DATA SHAPES**\n\n**Metrics Consistently Computed**:\n- **ρ (rho)**: Spearman rank correlation with F1\n- **SJ (Soft Jaccard)**: Structural consistency via Hungarian span matching\n- **FK (Fleiss Kappa)**: Surface-level entity agreement\n- **log-prob**: Sequence log-probability baseline\n- **AUROC**: Binary classification (good/bad output) at thresholds\n- **τ (Kendall tau)**: Rank correlation (in exp_012)\n- **p-values**: Statistical significance\n- **Oracle F1**: Best-of-N upper bound\n- **Headroom**: Oracle F1 - Greedy F1 (improvement potential)\n\n**Data Characteristics** (551 test instances, SciERC):\n- **NER**: ~529 instances with non-empty entities (22 filtered)\n- **RE**: ~397 instances with relations (154 filtered gold-empty)\n- **Sample F1 distribution**: Mean sample F1, std, pct_zero (fraction of samples with F1=0)\n- **Conditional filtering**: Excludes instances where ALL N samples have F1=0\n\n---\n\n### **6. SUPPORTING FILES**\n- **Memory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/memory.md` (lessons learned on offset hallucination, vLLM LoRA, OOM fixes)\n- **Paper Framing**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/paper_framing.md`\n- **ROADMAP**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/ROADMAP.md`\n- **Decisions Log**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/decisions.yaml`\n\n---\n\n### **7. ARTIFACT DIRECTORY STRUCTURE**\n```\nartifacts/\n├── evaluation.py              # Core metrics & correlation computation\n├── consistency.py             # SJ, κ, oracle metrics\n├── sampling.py               # vLLM + XGrammar sampling pipeline\n├── mvp_pilot_001/report/    # First MVP run (FAIL: RE ρ_sj=0.2535)\n├── mvp_pilot_004/report/    # Better model (FAIL: κ beats SJ on RE)\n├── exp_012_logprob_baseline/ # Log-prob baseline (SUCCESS: SJ wins NER decisively)\n├── ft_001/, ft_002/         # Fine-tuning artifacts\n└── _project/data/           # Project templates\n```\n\n---\n\nThis codebase implements a complete pipeline for **structured information extraction with self-consistency metrics**, with emphasis on NER-primary framing (SJ wins decisively on NER, ρ ≈ 0.36-0.39) and diagnostic understanding of why RE remains challenging (span-level SJ fundamentally lacks discriminative power for relations)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36d6115a-ae29-42f3-9a64-d29d87dc39c5","uuid":"4a0453f0-e78e-451b-8d61-4bdec63d6d85","timestamp":"2026-05-14T11:14:50.743Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1, I need to understand the existing experiment data and code structure. Search for:\n1. Any YAML/JSON files with experiment results or registry data\n2. Python scripts related to pilot experiments, especially anything computing rho, SJ, FK, log-prob, AUROC\n3. Any existing data directories (pilot_004, pilot_005, etc.)\n4. The experiment_plan file location\n5. Any analysis scripts or notebooks\n\nReport file paths and key contents (metrics, data shapes, etc). Be thorough - check directories like experiments/, data/, results/, scripts/, analysis/, src/, etc.","agentId":"a4d57eeefa224f3ae","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary of Experiment Data and Code Structure\n\nI've thoroughly explored the repository and compiled the following comprehensive report:\n\n### **1. EXPERIMENT PLAN FILE**\n- **Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/experiment_plan.yaml`\n- **Status**: Complete with prioritized experiments (P0, P1, P2)\n- **Key Experiments**:\n  - **exp-012** (baseline_logprob) — Make-or-break: compute sequence log-probability and correlate with F1 (ρ, AUROC, τ)\n  - 