dict**: Multiplicative penalty hypothesis REJECTED; problem is fundamental\n- **Diagnosis**: Span-level SJ lacks discriminative power for RE relations\n\n#### **exp_012_logprob_baseline** (DONE, SUCCESS)\n- **Purpose**: Baseline comparison for SJ against log-probability\n- **Key Results**:\n  - **NER Full (n=529)**: SJ ρ=0.3565 >> logprob ρ=0.1396, AUROC 0.689 vs 0.591\n  - **NER Cond (n=501)**: SJ ρ=0.4120 >> logprob ρ=0.1627, AUROC 0.706 vs 0.597\n  - **RE Full (n=397)**: logprob ρ=0.2467 > SJ ρ=0.2112 (marginal), but κ ρ=0.2528 beats both\n  - **RE Cond (n=296)**: SJ ρ=0.3683 >> logprob ρ=0.1457\n- **Metrics Computed**: Spearman ρ, Kendall τ, AUROC, p-values\n- **Report**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/exp_012_logprob_baseline/report/analysis_report.json`\n\n---\n\n### **4. REGISTRY & EXPERIMENT TRACKING**\n- **Location**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/registry.yaml`\n- **Experiments tracked**:\n  - ft_001, ft_002, ft_002_v2 (fine-tuning jobs)\n  - mvp_pilot_001/002/003/004/005 (MVP pilots)\n  - e1_component_wise_re_sj (diagnostic analysis)\n  - exp_012_logprob_baseline (log-prob baseline)\n- **Status tracking**: DONE/NEGATIVE/FAIL/SUCCESS with full metrics per experiment\n\n---\n\n### **5. KEY FINDINGS & DATA SHAPES**\n\n**Metrics Consistently Computed**:\n- **ρ (rho)**: Spearman rank correlation with F1\n- **SJ (Soft Jaccard)**: Structural consistency via Hungarian span matching\n- **FK (Fleiss Kappa)**: Surface-level entity agreement\n- **log-prob**: Sequence log-probability baseline\n- **AUROC**: Binary classification (good/bad output) at thresholds\n- **τ (Kendall tau)**: Rank correlation (in exp_012)\n- **p-values**: Statistical significance\n- **Oracle F1**: Best-of-N upper bound\n- **Headroom**: Oracle F1 - Greedy F1 (improvement potential)\n\n**Data Characteristics** (551 test instances, SciERC):\n- **NER**: ~529 instances with non-empty entities (22 filtered)\n- **RE**: ~397 instances with relations (154 filtered gold-empty)\n- **Sample F1 distribution**: Mean sample F1, std, pct_zero (fraction of samples with F1=0)\n- **Conditional filtering**: Excludes instances where ALL N samples have F1=0\n\n---\n\n### **6. SUPPORTING FILES**\n- **Memory**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/memory.md` (lessons learned on offset hallucination, vLLM LoRA, OOM fixes)\n- **Paper Framing**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/paper_framing.md`\n- **ROADMAP**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/ROADMAP.md`\n- **Decisions Log**: `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/decisions.yaml`\n\n---\n\n### **7. ARTIFACT DIRECTORY STRUCTURE**\n```\nartifacts/\n├── evaluation.py              # Core metrics & correlation computation\n├── consistency.py             # SJ, κ, oracle metrics\n├── sampling.py               # vLLM + XGrammar sampling pipeline\n├── mvp_pilot_001/report/    # First MVP run (FAIL: RE ρ_sj=0.2535)\n├── mvp_pilot_004/report/    # Better model (FAIL: κ beats SJ on RE)\n├── exp_012_logprob_baseline/ # Log-prob baseline (SUCCESS: SJ wins NER decisively)\n├── ft_001/, ft_002/         # Fine-tuning artifacts\n└── _project/data/           # Project templates\n```\n\n---\n\nThis codebase implements a complete pipeline for **structured information extraction with self-consistency metrics**, with emphasis on NER-primary framing (SJ wins decisively on NER, ρ ≈ 0.36-0.39) and diagnostic understanding of why RE remains challenging (span-level SJ fundamentally lacks discriminative power for relations)."}],"totalDurationMs":82617,"totalTokens":63729,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":59710,"output_tokens":2970,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},